#~ has no default, so it must come before
# A required parameter after an optional one could never be reached:
# arguments run in declaration order, and there is no notation for a
# hole to skip the optional with. Caught at the DECLARATION, where the
# mistake is, rather than at every call site that cannot be written.

fn f(a i32 = 1, b i32) i32
  return a + b
